#~ msgid "**Evidence still to confirm.** The reference to Brent (1976) in the footnote below, for bit-burst and the AGM logarithm, and the statement of the Jacobi identity for the nome, were written from memory and have not been checked against the sources; the owner will check them, and nothing in the design or in the code depends on them (the AGM is not used until its truncation bound is derived and proved here). The 1-ulp and 2-ulp widths quoted above come from the MPFR comparison, which is secondary evidence for the enclosures; the proof is the integer-bound argument in this section."
