#~ msgstr "Exact Dyadic Point の埋込み"

#~ msgid "`exact` means exact with respect to the supplied `BinFloat` value."
#~ msgstr "`exact` は supplied `BinFloat` に対して exact。Lower precision 指定時は bounds を outward に丸めます。"

#~ msgid "Build A Valid Range"
#~ msgstr "Valid Range の構築"

#~ msgid "Use `from_bounds` when endpoints are already known. Use `try_from_bounds` when input order or finiteness is not trusted."
#~ msgstr "Endpoint order/finiteness が untrusted なら `try_from_bounds`。`new(center,radius)` も storage は bounds です。"

#~ msgid "Enclose A Decimal Real Value Correctly"
#~ msgstr "Decimal Real を正しく包む"

#~ msgid "A nearest-rounded decimal-to-binary conversion followed by `exact` encloses only the resulting binary point. To enclose the original decimal, convert in both directions and use both bounds."
#~ msgstr "Nearest decimal-to-binary point + `exact` はその point だけを包みます。Original decimal は二方向変換します。"

#~ msgid "Use this pattern at decimal/binary boundaries, then keep calculations in the interval domain."
#~ msgstr "Representation boundary 後は interval domain 内で計算を続けます。"

#~ msgid "Read Set Relations"
#~ msgstr "Set Relation の読み方"

#~ msgid "Use `contains` for point inclusion, `subset`/`interior` for set containment, `overlap_state` for geometry, and `definitely_lt`/`definitely_gt` only when an order statement must hold for every point. Do not sort intervals with a scalar comparison rule."
#~ msgstr "`contains/subset/interior/overlap_state/definitely_lt` など set semantics を使い、scalar sort しません。"

#~ msgid "Perform Outward-Rounded Arithmetic"
#~ msgstr "Outward-Rounded Arithmetic"

#~ msgid "Use `BallContext` when endpoint precision/exponent limits and flags matter:"
#~ msgstr "Ordinary `+ - * /` は enclosure を保持。Denominator が interior zero crossing なら Entire、one-sided zero なら half-infinite。Endpoint precision/exponent/flags が必要なら `BallContext` と `*_ctx`。"

#~ msgid "Choose Total Or Checked Elementary Operations"
#~ msgstr "Total / Checked Elementary の選択"

#~ msgid "Total operations always return a valid enclosure. If certification cannot establish a tight trigonometric range, `sin_interval`/`cos_interval` may return `[-1, 1]`, and `tan_interval` may return Entire."
#~ msgstr "Proof/resource failure を観測するなら `try_*`、conservative range で続けるなら total API。 Correctness と tightness は別に `is_entire/width` で判定します。"

#~ msgid "Use Decorations When Domain Quality Matters"
#~ msgstr "Domain Quality に Decoration を使用"

#~ msgid "Decorations can weaken after domain clipping or discontinuity. NaI is distinct from Empty: NaI records an invalid decorated operation, while Empty is a valid set with no members."
#~ msgstr "Domain clipping/discontinuity は decoration を下げます。NaI は invalid decorated operation、Empty は valid set。"

#~ msgid "Recommended Practice"
#~ msgstr "推奨事項"

#~ msgid "Construct intervals from outward-rounded bounds at every representation boundary."
#~ msgstr "Representation boundary は outward bounds。"

#~ msgid "Keep all intermediate calculations in `BallFloat`; extracting a midpoint loses enclosure information."
#~ msgstr "Intermediate を BallFloat に保ち midpoint だけを抽出しない。"

#~ msgid "Use set relations rather than scalar equality/order."
#~ msgstr "Set relations を使う。"

#~ msgid "Decide explicitly whether proof failure should produce an error (`try_*`) or a conservative range (total API)."
#~ msgstr "Error または conservative range を明示選択。"

#~ msgid "Check width/Entire separately from correctness: an enclosure can be correct but too wide for the application."
#~ msgstr "Correctness 後に width/Entire を確認。"

#~ msgid "Use decorated intervals only when decoration/NaI semantics are actually part of the contract; otherwise bare intervals are simpler."
#~ msgstr "Contract が必要な場合だけ decorated interval。"

#~ msgid "[`ball_float_checked` tutorial](ball_float_checked.md) shows first-error construction and composition."
#~ msgstr "[Design](../design/ball_float.md)、[Conformance](../conformance/ball_float.md)、 [`ball_float_checked`](ball_float_checked.md) を参照してください。"

#~ msgid "`BallFloatResult` keeps `Result[BallFloat, ArithmeticError]` inside a fluent pipeline. Use it when invalid bounds, non-finite exact construction, or a checked elementary proof failure should stop later interval operations."
#~ msgstr "`BallFloatResult` は `Result[BallFloat,ArithmeticError]` を fluent pipeline に保持します。Invalid bounds、 non-finite exact source、checked elementary proof failure が後続 operation を止めます。"

#~ msgid "Validate Construction Once"
#~ msgstr "Construction を一度 Validate"

#~ msgid "Later operations short-circuit the first error. Use `map` for an infallible interval transform and `bind` when a callback may construct another checked interval. `flat_map` is deprecated."
#~ msgstr "Later operation は first error を short-circuit。Infallible は `map`、checked callback は `bind`。 `flat_map` は deprecated です。"

#~ msgid "Distinguish Wide Success From Failure"
#~ msgstr "Wide Success と Failure の区別"

#~ msgid "Entire is a valid success because it still encloses the mathematical result. For example, division by an interval crossing zero may produce Entire rather than `ArithmeticError`. After extracting a successful interval, apply an application tightness policy with `is_entire()`, `width()`, or boundedness."
#~ msgstr "Entire は valid enclosure success。Extract 後に `is_entire/width/boundedness` で application tightness policy を適用します。`contains/subset/overlaps` は extraction 後の bare interval に呼びます。"

#~ msgid "Decorations And Flags Stay Explicit"
#~ msgstr "Decoration / Flags は Explicit"

#~ msgid "`BallFloatResult` stores bare intervals only. It does not retain `BallFloatDecorated` state or `BallFlags`. Use raw `ball_float` APIs when decoration, NaI, inexact, overflow, or underflow is part of the result contract."
#~ msgstr "Wrapper は bare interval のみで `BallFloatDecorated`/`BallFlags` を保持しません。Decoration、NaI、 inexact/overflow/underflow が contract の場合は raw API を使います。"

